254
00:08:36,523 --> 00:08:38,293
It's very bejigeun.

255
00:08:39,393 --> 00:08:41,633
- "It's very bejigeun?"
- "Bejigeun?"

256
00:08:41,793 --> 00:08:43,333
"There's something fancy on top."

257
00:08:44,133 --> 00:08:47,733
Sir, what does "bejigeun" mean?

258
00:08:47,973 --> 00:08:48,973
It means rich.

259
00:08:48,973 --> 00:08:50,603
- Rich?
- Rich?

260
00:08:50,703 --> 00:08:52,303
It means that it's very rich.

261
00:08:52,303 --> 00:08:53,613
The flavor must be very rich.

262
00:08:53,613 --> 00:08:56,143
It must be an expensive place if it's something fancy.

263
00:08:56,143 --> 00:08:58,343
My favorite place in Jeju is...

264
00:08:58,343 --> 00:09:00,013
a place that sells whole plates of sea urchin roe.

265
00:09:00,013 --> 00:09:01,453
(Exclaiming)

266
00:09:01,613 --> 00:09:03,583
- That's the ultimate luxury.
- That sounds delicious.

267
00:09:03,583 --> 00:09:05,283
You can scoop up the sea urchin roe by the spoonful.

268
00:09:05,283 --> 00:09:07,653
(A restaurant where you can eat as much sea urchin roe as you want?)

269
00:09:07,823 --> 00:09:10,793
- Maybe the rich flavor comes...
- The rich flavor...

270
00:09:10,793 --> 00:09:13,023
- from sea urchin.
- It's very rich.

271
00:09:13,163 --> 00:09:14,893
- It's also fancy.
- Really?

272
00:09:14,893 --> 00:09:15,893
(Fancy, rich sea urchin?)

273
00:09:15,893 --> 00:09:17,303
Shall we get going?

274
00:09:17,733 --> 00:09:19,163
Sir, thank you for the drinks.

275
00:09:20,633 --> 00:09:22,133
I'm so curious. I love this.

276
00:09:23,743 --> 00:09:25,303
Could that be B-Side?

277
00:09:25,303 --> 00:09:26,713
Doesn't the lettering look like something...

278
00:09:26,713 --> 00:09:28,073
the production crew put up?

279
00:09:28,073 --> 00:09:29,813
- Where?
- "Thick doenjang paste."

280
00:09:29,813 --> 00:09:31,943
(A suspiciously placed menu name)

281
00:09:32,043 --> 00:09:33,613
Yes, that's the right way to look at it.

282
00:09:33,613 --> 00:09:35,053
That happens sometimes.

283
00:09:35,053 --> 00:09:37,223
- So Min has terrible instincts.
- Really?

284
00:09:37,383 --> 00:09:39,783
Once I get fixated on something, I can't let it go.

285
00:09:39,783 --> 00:09:41,253
I have to be careful not to get attached to an idea.

286
00:09:41,253 --> 00:09:42,323
So Min is...

287
00:09:42,553 --> 00:09:44,063
I get tunnel-visioned.

288
00:09:44,693 --> 00:09:46,563
- Gosh, look at the sea.
- It was a good approach.

289
00:09:46,563 --> 00:09:48,063
- It's beautiful.
- It's nice driving along the coast.

290
00:09:48,063 --> 00:09:49,063
This is lovely.

291
00:09:49,133 --> 00:09:51,163
- Oh, my.
- It's so picturesque.

292
00:09:51,263 --> 00:09:53,573
- It's beautiful.
- The sunlight isn't strong either.

293
00:09:53,573 --> 00:09:55,403
(The picturesque sea makes their hearts flutter.)

294
00:09:55,833 --> 00:09:57,573
I've been to Sehwa very often.

295
00:09:57,573 --> 00:09:59,803
- Really?
- Whenever I visited Jeju,

296
00:09:59,803 --> 00:10:01,173
I almost always stayed around this area.

297
00:10:01,173 --> 00:10:02,773
I've never been here before.

298
00:10:02,773 --> 00:10:04,713
I haven't been here before either.

299
00:10:05,183 --> 00:10:07,313
- Along the coastline, - Along the coastline?

300
00:10:07,313 --> 00:10:08,953
there are so many cute little shops.

301
00:10:08,953 --> 00:10:10,883
Exactly. It's the kind of place you want to stay.

302
00:10:11,523 --> 00:10:13,753
There are so many beautiful places these days.

303
00:10:13,753 --> 00:10:15,923
(Sehwa Village is filled with beautiful sights.)

304
00:10:16,293 --> 00:10:17,593
This must be it.

305
00:10:17,723 --> 00:10:18,793
- We're here.
- My gosh.

306
00:10:18,793 --> 00:10:19,923
- Is this it?
- What?

307
00:10:20,093 --> 00:10:21,133
Are we already here?

308
00:10:22,463 --> 00:10:23,463
- It's right next door.
- What's this?

309
00:10:23,463 --> 00:10:25,233
Wait, this is a famous place.

310
00:10:25,233 --> 00:10:26,503
- Really?
- This is...

311
00:10:26,503 --> 00:10:28,033
Isn't this Haenyeo's House?

312
00:10:28,033 --> 00:10:30,103
You're right. It's written "Haenyeo's House."

313
00:10:30,643 --> 00:10:32,573
They're known for seafood ramen. I mean, seafood ramyeon.

314
00:10:32,573 --> 00:10:33,743
- Seafood ramyeon?
- Seriously?

315
00:10:33,743 --> 00:10:36,113
I didn't mean seafood ramen. It's seafood ramyeon.

316
00:10:36,343 --> 00:10:37,683
Were you in Japan recently?

317
00:10:37,983 --> 00:10:39,313
- How did you know?
- "Seafood ramen."

318
00:10:39,313 --> 00:10:40,953
I was in Sapporo recently.

319
00:10:41,953 --> 00:10:43,553
Jeonsobari is hilarious.

320
00:10:43,553 --> 00:10:45,053
- Thank you.
- I'm sorry.

321
00:10:45,523 --> 00:10:48,723
(Crazy Lady returns.)

322
00:10:48,893 --> 00:10:50,263
This is amazing.

323
00:10:51,223 --> 00:10:52,393
I love it.

324
00:10:56,093 --> 00:10:58,263
- This is lovely.
- It's absolutely amazing.

325
00:10:58,263 --> 00:11:00,633
Gosh, this looks beautiful.

326
00:11:00,633 --> 00:11:01,733
It looks incredible.

327
00:11:01,733 --> 00:11:03,303
(The refreshing sea in Sehwa is a sight for sore eyes.)

328
00:11:03,473 --> 00:11:05,603
(Refreshing)

329
00:11:05,773 --> 00:11:07,113
It's been so long since I've seen the Jeju sea.

330
00:11:07,713 --> 00:11:09,013
The sea smell is lovely.

331
00:11:09,013 --> 00:11:10,813
- I love the fragrance of the sea.
- Right.

332
00:11:11,283 --> 00:11:13,343
- You said you didn't like it.
- I do.

333
00:11:13,483 --> 00:11:15,853
Jae Seok, you're putting on a show for the cameras.

334
00:11:15,853 --> 00:11:17,383
You said that you didn't like the sea.

335
00:11:17,383 --> 00:11:19,483
I said I don't like swimming in the ocean.

336
00:11:19,883 --> 00:11:21,453
- Okay?
- Okay.

337
00:11:21,453 --> 00:11:22,723
- Did you understand?
- Okay.

338
00:11:23,323 --> 00:11:24,993
"It's maendorong."

339
00:11:25,163 --> 00:11:27,063
Isn't it "they put something like this in here?"

340
00:11:27,163 --> 00:11:28,193
That's right.

341
00:11:28,193 --> 00:11:29,893
One of the hints was "it's maendorong."

342
00:11:30,163 --> 00:11:31,733
(First location: On-site reaction hint)

343
00:11:31,733 --> 00:11:34,303
(Gosh, they put something like this in here?)

344
00:11:34,303 --> 00:11:36,103
(It's maendorong.)

345
00:11:36,603 --> 00:11:40,143
(What exactly is this warm treasure?)

346
00:11:40,313 --> 00:11:42,243
One of the hints was "it's maendorong."

347
00:11:42,343 --> 00:11:43,583
"Welcome."

348
00:11:43,583 --> 00:11:44,913
But this place is so...

349
00:11:44,913 --> 00:11:47,383
This place is so famous.

350
00:11:47,483 --> 00:11:50,953
(Located right in front of Sehwa Beach)

351
00:11:51,523 --> 00:11:52,883
"Welcome."

352
00:11:52,883 --> 00:11:54,223
(With an exterior featuring a welcoming haenyeo)

353
00:11:54,553 --> 00:11:57,193
This place is so famous.

354
00:11:57,193 --> 00:11:58,963
(It has all the vibes of a trendy spot.)

355
00:11:59,393 --> 00:12:01,393
The food looks delicious.

356
00:12:01,393 --> 00:12:03,293
(And photos of mouthwatering dishes)

357
00:12:04,033 --> 00:12:05,763
Seafood ramyeon sounds amazing.

358
00:12:05,763 --> 00:12:07,773
- It'll be excellent.
- There's also abalone porridge.

359
00:12:08,133 --> 00:12:09,273
It looks delicious.

360
00:12:09,603 --> 00:12:11,243
Gosh, first of all...

361
00:12:12,443 --> 00:12:14,613
This looks like a tasty restaurant.

362
00:12:14,613 --> 00:12:15,973
- Yes.
- Right?

363
00:12:15,973 --> 00:12:17,743
- It has the tasty restaurant vibe.
- It has the vibe...

364
00:12:17,743 --> 00:12:18,943
of a famous, local food spot.

365
00:12:20,713 --> 00:12:23,353
(Welcome to the haenyeo restaurant.)

366
00:12:23,953 --> 00:12:25,283
(Traditional haenyeo diving suits hanging in one corner)

367
00:12:25,283 --> 00:12:27,193
There are tools used by the Haenyeos.

368
00:12:28,093 --> 00:12:32,423
(Even the buoy called tewak, worn by the passage of time)

369
00:12:33,493 --> 00:12:35,533
The ocean view is absolutely beautiful.

370
00:12:35,533 --> 00:12:37,733
(What's this place where you can enjoy the Jeju sea?)

371
00:12:37,963 --> 00:12:39,433
At this place...

372
00:12:39,433 --> 00:12:41,003
There's an old kerosene stove.

373
00:12:41,573 --> 00:12:43,203
I haven't seen that in a long time.

374
00:12:43,673 --> 00:12:45,243
- That's a kerosene stove.
- That's kerosene.

375
00:12:45,243 --> 00:12:46,503
There's kerosene inside.

376
00:12:46,503 --> 00:12:47,943
It runs on kerosene, so it works by itself?

377
00:12:47,943 --> 00:12:50,213
You light it using a wick.

378
00:12:50,443 --> 00:12:51,883
We used to cook with those.

379
00:12:51,883 --> 00:12:53,553
- That's so fascinating.
- We used that to cook with.

380
00:12:53,813 --> 00:12:55,113
(I'll make you ramyeon on the kerosene stove.)

381
00:12:56,153 --> 00:13:00,553
(The old stove that kept families of the1980s fed with warm meals)

382
00:13:00,553 --> 00:13:02,923
When you turned that on in the morning,

383
00:13:03,393 --> 00:13:04,763
the entire house smelled of kerosene.

384
00:13:04,893 --> 00:13:06,393
- Really?
- The smell of kerosene.

385
00:13:06,393 --> 00:13:07,963
That's fascinating.

386
00:13:08,293 --> 00:13:09,633
There's an old kerosene stove here.

387
00:13:09,633 --> 00:13:10,763
(What kind of restaurant is it with this nostalgic old stove?)

388
00:13:11,133 --> 00:13:13,203
I've been everywhere in this neighborhood.

389
00:13:13,873 --> 00:13:15,733
Why haven't I been to this place?

390
00:13:15,973 --> 00:13:18,143
They got a KBS sign here.

391
00:13:18,403 --> 00:13:20,473
- TV crews have been here.
- Right.

392
00:13:20,473 --> 00:13:22,413
It's been featured on TV.

393
00:13:22,413 --> 00:13:24,183
(A famous restaurant that's already been on TV?)

394
00:13:24,413 --> 00:13:26,143
If it's been on TV,

395
00:13:26,643 --> 00:13:28,953
maybe it's a real place.

396
00:13:28,953 --> 00:13:30,423
(Unbelievable)

397
00:13:30,423 --> 00:13:32,983
- If we keep it simple...
- That's simple-minded.

398
00:13:32,983 --> 00:13:34,553
You're bad at figuring things out.

399
00:13:34,723 --> 00:13:37,123
- You have to think directly.
- Just because it's been on TV...

400
00:13:37,123 --> 00:13:38,793
doesn't mean that it's real.

401
00:13:38,863 --> 00:13:40,733
What are you talking about?

402
00:13:40,733 --> 00:13:41,833
He's going straight for it.

403
00:13:41,833 --> 00:13:43,563
- Right.
- Exactly.

404
00:13:43,703 --> 00:13:45,203
Eun I, are you also from Jeolla Province?

405
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:47,133
My parents are from Jeolla Province.

406
00:13:47,733 --> 00:13:49,433
Gosh, seriously?

407
00:13:50,103 --> 00:13:51,143
Where are you from?

408
00:13:51,403 --> 00:13:53,403
I'm from Gyeonggi Province.

409
00:13:54,813 --> 00:13:55,813
Ilsan?

410
00:13:55,913 --> 00:13:58,143
- Yes, that's right.
- You're from Ilsan.

411
00:13:58,143 --> 00:13:59,213
- All right.
- Right.

412
00:13:59,783 --> 00:14:00,813
I can tell it's a popular restaurant,

413
00:14:00,813 --> 00:14:01,853
but what's so special about it?

414
00:14:01,853 --> 00:14:04,223
They offer unlimited rice and soup.

415
00:14:05,023 --> 00:14:07,253
They wouldn't have invited us here just for that.

416
00:14:07,253 --> 00:14:08,353
(Is unlimited refills the restaurant's big secret?)

417
00:14:09,153 --> 00:14:10,223
Ma'am?

418
00:14:10,823 --> 00:14:12,663
Yes, we're here.

419
00:14:13,323 --> 00:14:15,063
- She said, "We're here."
- "We're here?"

420
00:14:15,933 --> 00:14:18,203
It means "we're here" in Jeju dialect.

421
00:14:18,203 --> 00:14:19,263
(The owners appear with warm, welcoming smiles.)

422
00:14:19,263 --> 00:14:22,703
- Hi.
- Hi.

423
00:14:23,003 --> 00:14:24,243
How many...

424
00:14:24,943 --> 00:14:26,543
- Hi.
- Hi.

425
00:14:27,043 --> 00:14:28,273
- Welcome.
- Come over to this side, ma'am.

426
00:14:28,273 --> 00:14:29,513
- This side.
- Today...

427
00:14:29,513 --> 00:14:32,143
Stand between us, Sun Rye.

428
00:14:32,783 --> 00:14:33,783
(Breathing in)

429
00:14:33,783 --> 00:14:35,053
She's giving off fake vibes.

430
00:14:36,413 --> 00:14:39,053
I think she's a fake. She's acting.

431
00:14:39,053 --> 00:14:40,923
Anyway, ma'am.

432
00:14:40,923 --> 00:14:42,653
- We were born...
- Yes?

433
00:14:42,653 --> 00:14:44,363
- and raised on Jeju Island.
- I see.

434
00:14:44,363 --> 00:14:45,593
We then moved here, to Sehwa-ri,

435
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:46,793
- after getting married, - Okay.

436
00:14:46,793 --> 00:14:48,833
- and became the Lee family's...
- Yes?

437
00:14:48,833 --> 00:14:50,833
three daughters-in-law.

438
00:14:50,833 --> 00:14:52,733
Are you daughters-in-law?

439
00:14:52,733 --> 00:14:54,903
They're sisters-in-law.

440
00:14:55,303 --> 00:14:56,873
You're sisters-in-law, right?

441
00:14:57,403 --> 00:14:58,843
- Hi.
- Hi.

442
00:14:59,243 --> 00:15:02,313
We are running this haenyeo restaurant. I'm Oh Sun Rye.

443
00:15:02,313 --> 00:15:03,413
Lee Bok Nyeo.

444
00:15:03,413 --> 00:15:05,443
And I'm Kim Sun Geum.

445
00:15:05,583 --> 00:15:08,513
We're daughters-in-law of the same family.

446
00:15:08,653 --> 00:15:10,013
I'm the eldest daughter-in-law.

447
00:15:10,013 --> 00:15:11,483
(Diver 1, the eldest daughter-in-law)

448
00:15:11,483 --> 00:15:12,623
I'm the second.

449
00:15:12,623 --> 00:15:13,893
(Diver 2, the 2nd daughter-in-law)

450
00:15:13,893 --> 00:15:15,453
And I'm the third.

451
00:15:15,453 --> 00:15:16,553
(The cook, the youngest daughter-in-law)

452
00:15:16,553 --> 00:15:18,093
We're sisters-in-law.

453
00:15:18,093 --> 00:15:19,993
(Sehwa-ri's haenyeo trio of sisters-in-law)

454
00:15:21,533 --> 00:15:24,133
Since we were born and raised at the villages by the sea,

455
00:15:24,303 --> 00:15:28,373
seventy percent of the women here became divers.

456
00:15:29,003 --> 00:15:31,743
I learned how to dive in Sehwa...

457
00:15:31,743 --> 00:15:34,043
and have been diving for 45 years.

458
00:15:34,043 --> 00:15:35,773
(Veteran haenyeo with over 45 years of experience)

459
00:15:35,773 --> 00:15:40,853
It's become harder for us to dive for seafood as we've gotten older.

460
00:15:41,483 --> 00:15:45,723
So we decided to open a restaurant serving the seafood we caught.

461
00:15:46,883 --> 00:15:49,793
(And that's how the haenyeo restaurant began!)

462
00:15:49,893 --> 00:15:52,163
How long have you been running this place?

463
00:15:52,163 --> 00:15:56,133
We first started in front of the museum,

464
00:15:56,133 --> 00:15:58,203
then moved here about two years ago.

465
00:15:58,803 --> 00:16:00,333
- So this is a new place.
- It's only been two years.

466
00:16:00,333 --> 00:16:01,873
It's only been two years,

467
00:16:01,873 --> 00:16:03,203
but So Min said this was...

468
00:16:03,203 --> 00:16:05,143
a long-established, famous restaurant.

469
00:16:06,803 --> 00:16:08,643
Our first restaurant got famous. And we moved here.

470
00:16:08,643 --> 00:16:09,713
That's why she thought like that.

471
00:16:10,643 --> 00:16:12,183
So Min sounded as if...

472
00:16:12,183 --> 00:16:14,613
she knew this place well, and I believed her.

473
00:16:14,613 --> 00:16:15,883
Is that so?

474
00:16:15,883 --> 00:16:19,323
Which dish is out of the ordinary?

475
00:16:19,783 --> 00:16:21,353
As for our menu...

476
00:16:21,893 --> 00:16:23,053
Our soup is seaweed japguk.

477
00:16:23,323 --> 00:16:24,423
- Seaweed...
- Seaweed...

478
00:16:24,423 --> 00:16:25,663
Seaweed japguk.

479
00:16:25,663 --> 00:16:26,723
- Japguk?
- Japguk?

480
00:16:26,723 --> 00:16:30,233
It's called seaweed japguk. Here's what goes inside it.

481
00:16:30,233 --> 00:16:32,133
It's the dish...

482
00:16:32,133 --> 00:16:35,773
our parents cooked for us when we were growing up.

483
00:16:35,773 --> 00:16:38,173
What our grandmothers cooked for us.

484
00:16:38,503 --> 00:16:41,213
Sea hare, sea snails, top shells, limpets...

485
00:16:41,213 --> 00:16:43,883
- A variety.
- Yes, it's a variety of seafood.

486
00:16:43,883 --> 00:16:45,313
- It sounds good.
- It sounds good.

487
00:16:45,313 --> 00:16:47,313
- For real.
- Just as our children...

488
00:16:47,313 --> 00:16:48,313
My gosh.

489
00:16:48,313 --> 00:16:50,523
helped themselves to a bowl, we cook a big pot...

490
00:16:50,523 --> 00:16:52,683
so customers can have as much as they like.

491
00:16:52,683 --> 00:16:53,893
(Customers still get unlimited refills today.)

492
00:16:53,893 --> 00:16:55,893
- That's why it's in a big pot.
- That's why.

493
00:16:56,023 --> 00:16:57,593
The soup is over there.

494
00:16:57,593 --> 00:16:59,963
- Just like at your house.
- That's right.

495
00:16:59,963 --> 00:17:00,993
(Bringing back memories of meals at home long ago...)

496
00:17:01,133 --> 00:17:04,533
Seaweed japguk has been enjoyed for a long time.

497
00:17:05,163 --> 00:17:10,003
In the past, haenyeo would sell the expensive seafood they caught...

498
00:17:10,703 --> 00:17:13,343
and cook the cheaper seafood for themselves at home.

499
00:17:15,473 --> 00:17:18,243
Now, seafood has become harder to come by,

500
00:17:18,243 --> 00:17:21,183
so this isn't a dish you can easily find anymore.

501
00:17:21,183 --> 00:17:22,783
(Seaweed japguk filled them up after a day of diving.)

502
00:17:23,413 --> 00:17:27,293
(Haenyeo comfort food filled with memories of those days)

503
00:17:27,293 --> 00:17:30,023
A special spread featuring the bounty of Jeju's sea.

504
00:17:30,023 --> 00:17:32,023
A set meal you can only find on Jeju,

505
00:17:32,023 --> 00:17:34,693
prepared by three haenyeo sisters-in-law.

506
00:17:34,693 --> 00:17:36,133
(A must-visit for tourists on Jeju)

