762
00:26:35,573 --> 00:26:36,873
"It's coming right up."

763
00:26:36,873 --> 00:26:38,573
- I was surprised.
- How...

764
00:26:39,003 --> 00:26:40,273
How did they know?

765
00:26:40,273 --> 00:26:42,013
We had a hunch you'd order it.

766
00:26:42,013 --> 00:26:43,843
- I was genuinely surprised.
- Same here.

767
00:26:43,843 --> 00:26:45,343
- Jae Seok.
- It was a joke.

768
00:26:45,813 --> 00:26:47,613
- I thought you pre-ordered it.
- For real.

769
00:26:47,613 --> 00:26:48,683
Wait.

770
00:26:49,213 --> 00:26:50,853
- You were joking, right?
- Yes.

771
00:26:50,953 --> 00:26:52,053
Here it comes.

772
00:26:52,053 --> 00:26:54,253
- Ma'am.
- Here's your seafood ramyeon.

773
00:26:54,323 --> 00:26:56,593
(Excited)

774
00:26:56,593 --> 00:26:57,993
- Ma'am.
- Oh, my.

775
00:26:57,993 --> 00:26:59,123
(The noodle maniac stands up.)

776
00:26:59,123 --> 00:27:00,623
- This place is real.
- It looks bomb.

777
00:27:01,793 --> 00:27:02,833
It's real.

778
00:27:02,833 --> 00:27:06,033
(Here's the octopus ramyeon!)

779
00:27:06,303 --> 00:27:08,103
(Jeju octopus fresh from the sea)

780
00:27:08,103 --> 00:27:10,003
I caught an octopus!

781
00:27:11,073 --> 00:27:13,603
The octopus was caught this morning.

782
00:27:13,603 --> 00:27:14,643
My gosh.

783
00:27:14,713 --> 00:27:17,113
- This place is real.
- It's real.

784
00:27:17,313 --> 00:27:18,413
This place is real.

785
00:27:18,413 --> 00:27:19,483
(Just looking at it makes their mouths water.)

786
00:27:21,083 --> 00:27:24,753
(Octopus ramyeon)

787
00:27:24,753 --> 00:27:25,923
This octopus is bigger.

788
00:27:25,923 --> 00:27:28,653
- That one?
- I made it with today's big catch.

789
00:27:28,653 --> 00:27:30,153
But that one's small.

790
00:27:30,423 --> 00:27:32,323
- Did you buy the octopus?
- No.

791
00:27:32,323 --> 00:27:33,563
(No!)

792
00:27:33,563 --> 00:27:35,593
- I'm not lying.
- She's...

793
00:27:35,763 --> 00:27:36,893
The owner is adorable.

794
00:27:37,833 --> 00:27:38,933
Try it.

795
00:27:38,933 --> 00:27:40,403
(How will the fresh octopus ramyeon taste?)

796
00:27:40,403 --> 00:27:42,633
- It's...
- My goodness. I'm digging in.

797
00:27:42,633 --> 00:27:43,633
(No words are needed.)

798
00:27:43,633 --> 00:27:45,703
I visited Jeju Island a few years ago.

799
00:27:46,003 --> 00:27:48,613
(I'm doing just fine eating on my own.)

800
00:27:48,713 --> 00:27:49,743
This is...

801
00:27:49,743 --> 00:27:51,013
(Even a single piece of octopus is huge.)

802
00:27:51,013 --> 00:27:52,213
It's really...

803
00:27:52,213 --> 00:27:53,383
(My gosh, it's plump.)

804
00:27:57,013 --> 00:27:58,223
It was caught today.

805
00:27:58,823 --> 00:28:01,053
- The owner...
- It's today's catch.

806
00:28:01,993 --> 00:28:03,553
A competent vet could bring it back to life.

807
00:28:05,593 --> 00:28:07,493
It could come back to life with CPR.

808
00:28:07,493 --> 00:28:08,693
This is bad.

809
00:28:08,733 --> 00:28:10,633
(Drinking from the bowl)

810
00:28:11,533 --> 00:28:12,563
(This is bad.)

811
00:28:12,563 --> 00:28:14,163
- Why?
- How do we move on?

812
00:28:15,003 --> 00:28:17,603
Jae Seok trusts a place if it serves instant noodles.

813
00:28:17,733 --> 00:28:19,043
(Busted)

814
00:28:19,043 --> 00:28:20,103
- Right?
- Instant noodles...

815
00:28:20,103 --> 00:28:21,343
This place is real.

816
00:28:23,513 --> 00:28:24,613
(Octopus ramyeon wins his trust.)

817
00:28:24,613 --> 00:28:25,683
For real.

818
00:28:26,883 --> 00:28:28,853
- When my dad...
- Yes?

819
00:28:28,853 --> 00:28:30,353
lived on Jeju Island,

820
00:28:30,683 --> 00:28:32,753
he caught an octopus while he was peeing.

821
00:28:32,753 --> 00:28:35,353
So he caught an octopus while taking a walk?

822
00:28:35,493 --> 00:28:37,293
No, he was literally peeing.

823
00:28:37,653 --> 00:28:39,323
I was trying to make it sound nice.

824
00:28:39,323 --> 00:28:41,393
The octopus came out because of the heat.

825
00:28:41,393 --> 00:28:42,933
(The octopus couldn't handle her dad's body heat.)

826
00:28:42,933 --> 00:28:44,363
Your dad's...

827
00:28:44,603 --> 00:28:46,263
If you don't mind me asking,

828
00:28:46,963 --> 00:28:48,673
is he actually that hot?

829
00:28:48,673 --> 00:28:51,443
(Is he actually that hot?)

830
00:28:52,503 --> 00:28:56,143
(A passionate man whose heat overpowered the sea)

831
00:28:56,143 --> 00:28:58,383
(Crying with laughter at the thought of her dad)

832
00:28:58,783 --> 00:29:01,043
- I personally know So Min's dad.
- You do.

833
00:29:01,213 --> 00:29:03,913
He's a funny talker.

834
00:29:04,083 --> 00:29:06,523
The sea has its own water temperature.

835
00:29:07,953 --> 00:29:10,253
My dad said it came out because of the heat.

836
00:29:10,393 --> 00:29:12,623
Before he could zip his pants up, my dad caught the octopus.

837
00:29:12,723 --> 00:29:14,493
I caught an octopus!

838
00:29:14,563 --> 00:29:17,963
(Shocked)

839
00:29:17,963 --> 00:29:19,433
- So Min's dad...
- When I was young...

840
00:29:19,703 --> 00:29:21,373
Her dad's a funny talker.

841
00:29:21,903 --> 00:29:23,533
I still remember it. I was there...

842
00:29:23,533 --> 00:29:25,803
when I was six. I can still remember it.

843
00:29:26,103 --> 00:29:28,313
If this place is fake, no other place could be real.

844
00:29:28,313 --> 00:29:30,473
- Exactly.
- This place is real, period.

845
00:29:30,473 --> 00:29:32,213
(Haenyeo feast)

846
00:29:32,383 --> 00:29:34,513
It's hard to believe this place could be fake.

847
00:29:34,513 --> 00:29:37,213
I felt it was real from the taste.

848
00:29:37,353 --> 00:29:38,853
- More than anything, - Yes?

849
00:29:39,223 --> 00:29:42,223
I could see earnestness in the owners' eyes.

850
00:29:42,623 --> 00:29:44,663
- I saw integrity in their eyes.
- That's a bad approach, Yunho.

851
00:29:44,663 --> 00:29:48,033
Yunho, that's too much of an emotional approach.

852
00:29:48,333 --> 00:29:49,463
But I'm an emotional person.

853
00:29:49,793 --> 00:29:50,863
I am too.

854
00:29:52,533 --> 00:29:53,663
Same here.

855
00:29:53,803 --> 00:29:55,433
- Me too.
- Me too.

856
00:29:55,433 --> 00:29:56,573
- There are a lot of us here.
- You too?

857
00:29:56,573 --> 00:29:58,443
- I'm the only thinker.
- A thinker?

858
00:29:59,073 --> 00:30:00,703
I'm an absolute thinker.

859
00:30:01,413 --> 00:30:02,613
- Absolute thinker?
- Yes.

860
00:30:02,613 --> 00:30:04,013
The way they saw us off...

861
00:30:04,013 --> 00:30:05,643
- proves they're real.
- Right?

862
00:30:05,643 --> 00:30:07,283
- Earlier...
- For real.

863
00:30:07,283 --> 00:30:08,283
Right?

864
00:30:08,283 --> 00:30:10,453
I hope the place is real.

865
00:30:10,513 --> 00:30:12,253
The eldest owner came and said,

866
00:30:12,253 --> 00:30:14,953
"Take care, okay? That's all I can say to you."

867
00:30:14,953 --> 00:30:17,123
- Really.
- "Win the grand prize this year!"

868
00:30:17,493 --> 00:30:18,923
I hope everything goes well for you.

869
00:30:18,923 --> 00:30:19,923
Thank you.

870
00:30:19,923 --> 00:30:21,793
- Keep reaching for the stars.
- Thank you.

871
00:30:22,563 --> 00:30:25,203
- Win the grand prize this year.
- Thank you.

872
00:30:25,763 --> 00:30:27,703
If the place is fake, she was lying.

873
00:30:28,003 --> 00:30:30,473
But her feelings weren't fake.

874
00:30:30,473 --> 00:30:31,543
(The deduction which can be done from an emotional person)

875
00:30:31,543 --> 00:30:32,573
Is that so?

876
00:30:33,173 --> 00:30:35,113
- She was sincere.
- Her words made me happy.

877
00:30:35,113 --> 00:30:37,843
That place is real in my heart.

878
00:30:37,843 --> 00:30:39,043
It should be real.

879
00:30:39,883 --> 00:30:41,083
What could the fritters be?

880
00:30:41,083 --> 00:30:43,913
Deep-fry anything, and it's good.

881
00:30:44,923 --> 00:30:46,223
(Second location: On-site reaction hint)

882
00:30:46,223 --> 00:30:47,453
(Even the aroma is different.)

883
00:30:47,453 --> 00:30:49,023
(They deep-fried all of Jeju Island.)

884
00:30:49,193 --> 00:30:50,693
(Kosirong haemjjeo.)

885
00:30:51,193 --> 00:30:53,523
For some reason, fritter places are...

886
00:30:54,223 --> 00:30:56,593
- They're the easiest to fake.
- It's the easiest.

887
00:30:57,233 --> 00:30:59,563
Doesn't this place look like a residential area...

888
00:30:59,563 --> 00:31:01,263
near the coast?

889
00:31:02,303 --> 00:31:04,233
I can't expect a restaurant here.

890
00:31:04,233 --> 00:31:05,303
Exactly.

891
00:31:05,373 --> 00:31:07,073
- We're here.
- We're here.

892
00:31:07,373 --> 00:31:08,673
- The area is...
- We're here.

893
00:31:09,073 --> 00:31:10,073
(Excited)

894
00:31:10,073 --> 00:31:11,243
(Shuffling with excitement)

895
00:31:11,243 --> 00:31:12,243
(Breathing in)

896
00:31:12,243 --> 00:31:14,113
The weather is on point.

897
00:31:17,213 --> 00:31:18,923
Really, today's sky and all are...

898
00:31:18,923 --> 00:31:20,783
(Sehwa Village in Jeju Island is bursting with refreshing scenery.)

899
00:31:21,083 --> 00:31:22,623
That's a carrot field right out front.

900
00:31:22,623 --> 00:31:25,023
(Sehwa's carrot fields stretch as far as the eye can see.)

901
00:31:25,593 --> 00:31:27,663
Nice. Even the weather is perfect.

902
00:31:27,663 --> 00:31:28,963
(What's the second treasure awaiting them in Sehwa Village?)

903
00:31:30,193 --> 00:31:31,403
Welfare center?

904
00:31:31,403 --> 00:31:33,803
(Welfare center?)

905
00:31:34,363 --> 00:31:35,503
Welfare center?

906
00:31:35,503 --> 00:31:38,903
(The second restaurant is...)

907
00:31:38,903 --> 00:31:40,043
(a welfare center?)

908
00:31:40,043 --> 00:31:41,413
What kind of place is this?

909
00:31:45,113 --> 00:31:46,183
Buckwheat.

910
00:31:46,743 --> 00:31:47,883
There's a restaurant over there.

911
00:31:48,013 --> 00:31:49,053
- What is it?
- Buckwheat.

912
00:31:49,683 --> 00:31:52,183
(The welfare center houses...)

913
00:31:52,183 --> 00:31:53,753
(a buckwheat restaurant!)

914
00:31:53,753 --> 00:31:54,993
But wasn't it fritters?

915
00:31:55,793 --> 00:31:57,193
Deep-fried buckwheat noodles?

916
00:31:57,853 --> 00:31:59,393
- It sounds good.
- No way.

917
00:31:59,393 --> 00:32:01,593
Just the thought of deep-fried noodles is delicious.

918
00:32:01,593 --> 00:32:04,463
(Could deep-fried buckwheat noodles be the fragrant taste of Jeju?)

919
00:32:04,463 --> 00:32:06,703
It's interesting how it's in the welfare center.

920
00:32:06,703 --> 00:32:08,203
(But a restaurant inside a welfare center...)

921
00:32:08,203 --> 00:32:11,203
Right? It's a welfare center. Why is there a restaurant in here?

922
00:32:12,243 --> 00:32:14,813
The village chief's name is on here.

923
00:32:15,673 --> 00:32:17,473
(Welfare Center)

924
00:32:17,473 --> 00:32:19,043
What kind of place is this? I'm curious.

925
00:32:19,043 --> 00:32:20,713
(What kind of restaurant could it be?)

926
00:32:20,843 --> 00:32:23,783
(They head inside to find out.)

927
00:32:23,783 --> 00:32:24,953
A buckwheat mill?

928
00:32:26,093 --> 00:32:27,093
(Welfare Center)

929
00:32:27,093 --> 00:32:28,093
(What kind of restaurant could it be?)

930
00:32:28,093 --> 00:32:29,733
What kind of place is this? I'm curious.

931
00:32:29,733 --> 00:32:31,233
(What kind of restaurant could it be?)

932
00:32:31,393 --> 00:32:34,303
(They head inside to find out.)

933
00:32:34,303 --> 00:32:35,433
A buckwheat mill?

934
00:32:36,573 --> 00:32:37,603
(Surprised)

935
00:32:38,303 --> 00:32:40,543
- There's a mill here.
- Goodness.

936
00:32:40,543 --> 00:32:42,573
(A mill inside the restaurant?)

937
00:32:43,910 --> 00:32:45,720
- There's a buckwheat mill.
- Right?

938
00:32:45,780 --> 00:32:47,020
For making flour.

939
00:32:47,750 --> 00:32:49,190
- Right?
- For making flour.

940
00:32:49,450 --> 00:32:53,490
(A scoop! Correspondent BIBI is on the scene.)

941
00:32:53,490 --> 00:32:54,520
(BIBI, Jeju correspondent)

942
00:32:54,520 --> 00:32:55,830
It's so cool.

943
00:32:56,560 --> 00:32:59,100
I wasn't sure what to expect since it's a welfare center,

944
00:32:59,100 --> 00:33:00,330
but it's a restaurant.

945
00:33:00,330 --> 00:33:01,970
(Inside, it's a proper restaurant!)

946
00:33:02,530 --> 00:33:04,630
- Over there.
- A foot bath over there!

947
00:33:05,140 --> 00:33:06,240
- What?
- What?

948
00:33:06,440 --> 00:33:07,440
A foot bath?

949
00:33:07,440 --> 00:33:08,970
- What?
- No way.

950
00:33:09,570 --> 00:33:11,110
(What's a foot bath doing in a restaurant?)

951
00:33:11,110 --> 00:33:12,540
It really is a foot bath.

952
00:33:13,940 --> 00:33:15,350
- What's that?
- What's this?

953
00:33:16,310 --> 00:33:17,580
- No way.
- It's a foot bath.

954
00:33:17,580 --> 00:33:19,280
You can soak your feet here.

955
00:33:19,280 --> 00:33:20,880
(BIBI, Jeju correspondent)

956
00:33:21,080 --> 00:33:22,790
Then do they deep-fry our feet?

957
00:33:23,450 --> 00:33:25,460
- Our feet...
- What do they deep-fry?

958
00:33:25,460 --> 00:33:27,960
- I feel so drained.
- What do they deep-fry?

959
00:33:28,090 --> 00:33:29,330
- Eun I.
- Let's sit down.

960
00:33:29,490 --> 00:33:31,660
- What do they deep-fry?
- Why'd they deep-fry our feet?

961
00:33:31,660 --> 00:33:33,000
They deep-fry something.

962
00:33:34,030 --> 00:33:36,230
It just looks so suspicious.

963
00:33:36,470 --> 00:33:39,170
- Exactly. It's just...
- This is so...

964
00:33:39,270 --> 00:33:41,240
(Peeking)

965
00:33:41,810 --> 00:33:43,140
This is impossible.

966
00:33:44,310 --> 00:33:48,110
This just looks like a welfare center.

967
00:33:48,880 --> 00:33:49,950
That's impossible.

968
00:33:50,110 --> 00:33:51,250
(I caught you!)

969
00:33:51,250 --> 00:33:53,150
I think this is just a welfare center.

970
00:33:53,620 --> 00:33:55,350
It was just a welfare center.

971
00:33:55,350 --> 00:33:56,750
I think they decorated it fake.

972
00:33:56,750 --> 00:33:59,460
(Is this a fake shop which made use of a welfare center?)

973
00:33:59,620 --> 00:34:01,420
They must've made that fake foot bath.

974
00:34:01,420 --> 00:34:03,290
- This?
- Yes, I think they made this.

975
00:34:03,730 --> 00:34:06,700
They laid water pipes to make this.

976
00:34:06,700 --> 00:34:08,200
See if the water runs.

977
00:34:09,370 --> 00:34:11,270
- It works. The water runs.
- The water runs.

978
00:34:11,570 --> 00:34:13,500
They have this in a welfare center?

979
00:34:13,640 --> 00:34:15,570
They must've made this.

980
00:34:15,570 --> 00:34:17,970
(What is Jeju's hidden treasure here?)

981
00:34:18,170 --> 00:34:19,840
Let's invite the owner.

982
00:34:21,180 --> 00:34:22,980
- Hello.
- Hello.

983
00:34:22,980 --> 00:34:24,450
- Hello.
- Hello.

984
00:34:24,510 --> 00:34:26,750
(Lee Sang Heon, the owner)

985
00:34:26,920 --> 00:34:29,890
The first thing that caught my attention is the foot bath.

986
00:34:29,990 --> 00:34:30,990
Right.

987
00:34:30,990 --> 00:34:32,590
Do people get the foot bath and eat here?

988
00:34:34,060 --> 00:34:35,990
This is a welfare center...

989
00:34:36,190 --> 00:34:37,590
run by the village.

990
00:34:37,760 --> 00:34:38,930
(So it is a welfare center.)

991
00:34:38,930 --> 00:34:40,030
So...

992
00:34:40,460 --> 00:34:42,700
They can have a foot bath after they farm,

993
00:34:42,700 --> 00:34:45,600
and tourists who come back from walking the Olle Trail...

994
00:34:45,900 --> 00:34:48,470
can have a foot bath as they eat.

995
00:34:49,110 --> 00:34:51,010
We made use of the welfare center...

996
00:34:51,140 --> 00:34:53,440
to introduce Jeju's buckwheat to them.

997
00:34:53,440 --> 00:34:55,250
That's how we started running this restaurant.

998
00:34:56,050 --> 00:34:58,080
- That's a great idea.
- It's amazing.

999
00:34:58,650 --> 00:35:00,750
Gujwa is famous for other things,

1000
00:35:00,750 --> 00:35:02,720
such as Sehwa Village, so why buckwheat?

1001
00:35:02,820 --> 00:35:04,520
Do you know Korea's...

1002
00:35:04,520 --> 00:35:06,890
leading producing region of buckwheat?

1003
00:35:06,890 --> 00:35:08,260
Isn't it Bongpyeong?

1004
00:35:08,430 --> 00:35:11,460
Most people think it's Bongpyeong.

1005
00:35:11,700 --> 00:35:15,030
Actually, the leading producing region is here, Jeju Island.

1006
00:35:15,030 --> 00:35:16,400
- Really?
- Is that so?

1007
00:35:16,770 --> 00:35:19,000
And I'm a farmer chef.

1008
00:35:19,340 --> 00:35:21,840
- A farmer chef.
- He's a farmer and a chef.

1009
00:35:21,840 --> 00:35:23,010
- And a chef.
- Yes.

1010
00:35:23,140 --> 00:35:26,380
The hint said you deep-fry something.

1011
00:35:26,380 --> 00:35:28,950
- Right.
- We sell pork cutlets.

1012
00:35:29,110 --> 00:35:31,450
It's a bit different from the common pork cutlet.

1013
00:35:31,650 --> 00:35:32,750
How so?

1014
00:35:32,750 --> 00:35:34,520
(The pork cutlet is different?)

1015
00:35:34,520 --> 00:35:36,520
Firstly, we use Jeju black pork.

1016
00:35:36,520 --> 00:35:37,750
- Really?
- This...

1017
00:35:38,120 --> 00:35:40,190
I really love pork cutlet.

1018
00:35:40,190 --> 00:35:41,460
Me too. It's going to be delicious.

1019
00:35:41,460 --> 00:35:43,230
(Pork cutlet lovers are excited.)

1020
00:35:43,330 --> 00:35:44,690
It uses some buckwheat too.

1021
00:35:44,690 --> 00:35:48,530
